t so far that you cannot  fetch it back  the tale of the man in the wolf is a  fairly short story but there is more  than meets the eye it's not just a  simple tale of a wolf attacking a man in  this story we have one party learning a  lesson while being observed by another I  mean how many times have you told a  friend or family member not to do  something only to watch them do it  anyway  completely disregarding your warning we  have the Fox who is clearly quite clever  and essentially understands its position  in the food chain  man is very clearly the ultimate  predator and the Fox does not wish to  challenge this fact the wolf however is  far more prideful and refuses to listen  to the Fox boasting that if he ever came  across a man he would set upon him the  Fox predicting the outcome teaches the  wolf a lesson by taking him to a man and  watching as the wolf fails miserably in  his attempts to overpower the man there  are a few meanings and lessons I took  away from this story the first being to  know your surroundings and limitations  which will in turn stop you overreaching  in the same ways the wolf did the second  theme being that you never really know  how you will react in any given  situation until you are placed in that  very situation you may know yourself  pretty well but if you don't know the  situation it's almost impossible to say  the wolf for example is undoubtedly  aware that it's a very strong animal but  it boasts about been in the situation  then it's never been in before  completely disregarding the advice and  experience of the Fox and this becomes  evident in the fact that the Fox has to  point out to the wharf what a man even  looks like the wolf being aware of his  own strength was clearly non enough in  this situation as he was not prepared  for the man's gun or knife and it almost  lost his life as a result the message  here seems to be quite simple do not  brag about how you would react in  scenarios that you've never been in  befor